DESCRIPTION:Born in the wake of China’s controversial one-child policy\,
  six-year-old Wang Juan (Cao Ruofan) finds her life completely upended by 
 her mother’s pregnancy. The young girl is soon taken from her rural home
 —where kite flying and swimming fill her days—and brought to the home 
 of a discordant\, childless couple. Abandoned in an unfamiliar city with h
 er new legal guardians\, Juan strives to find a sense of belonging\, a str
 uggle that only worsens when she’s uprooted twice more before turning ei
 ghteen. Anchored by a powerful performance from Resurrection ’s Li Gengx
 i\, who plays teenage Juan\, Zou Jing’s confident debut is an achingly t
 ender coming-of-age drama. And while it never shies away from the \nCatego
 ry: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/3331
 74-film-screening-a-girl-unknown
