CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The winner of the Jury Prize at this year’s Cannes Film Fest
 ival\, German director Valeska Grisebach’s first feature since 2017’s 
 Western deftly shape-shifts between genres. Yana Radeva plays Veska\, a Bu
 lgarian archeologist who runs into an old love\, Said (Syuleyman Letifov)
 \, who is involved in some legally murky business dealings. When he goes m
 issing\, Veska investigates\, leading to a labyrinthine border town myster
 y full of intrigue and local color. The Dreamed Adventure finds Grisebach 
 once again working with a nonprofessional cast to create a film with the g
 rit of a Western and the scope of Chinatown . One could happily get lost i
 n the movie’s intoxicating atmosphere—or instead focus on R\nCategory:
  Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/333175-
 film-screening-the-dreamed-adventure
