BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Research Fundamentals: Organize Your Research — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261013T120000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261013T125000
DTSTAMP:20261011T191501Z
UID:4a5ab20a886d87e9c5c99483e348@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\,Providence\,
 United States
DESCRIPTION:You’ve gathered sources and evaluated them—but how do you 
 keep everything organized as your project grows? How do you move smoothly 
 from researching to writing when you have dozens of PDFs and scattered not
 es? Join librarians as we tackle these practical challenges in our Organiz
 e Your Research Workshop. We’ll explore note-taking strategies and tools
  that support long-term research\, walk through how to compose annotated b
 ibliographies that do real intellectual work\, and discuss organizational 
 frameworks that help you map your informational needs\, track progress\, a
 nd recognize gaps in your evidence base. Event registration is preferred. 
 Please contact micah_saxton@brown.edu with any questions\nCategory: Lectur
 es\, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/li
