UID:e063bba35a4905a578ebdfe54368@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:The development of animal law is impacted by the work of schol
 ars\, professors\, judges\, legislators\, and lobbyists.  It is also affe
 cted by the work of animal activists.  Their work raises many questions i
 ncluding the legality of their methods\, the accuracy of their critiques\,
  and the efficacy of their proposed solutions.  It can be complicated to 
 teach about the work of activists in law schools.  This panel will explor
 e some of the contours of this activism and how it can be addressed in ani
 mal law courses\, noting that some classes lend themselves more readily to
  this exploration. Join us for an insightful conversation with our panelis
 ts\, Will Lowrey\, Steffen Seitz\, Amanda Elyse\, and our mod\nCategory: L
 ectures & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/the-c
 hallenges-of-teaching-about-animal-activism-adjunct-teachers-in-animal-law
LOCATION:George Washington University\, Washington\, DC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
