DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261015T130000
DTSTAMP:20261011T191501Z
UID:d9eedf0ffdc9109587c4af8c8f67@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A webinar panel discussion with Prof. Ara Merjian (Italian Stu
 dies\, NYU) and Joyce Tsai (Director\, Clyfford Still Museum) About the Ex
 hibition: The 1920s emerged as a decade suspended between collapse and rec
 onstruction\, an era marked by “cracks and reforms” that ushered in a 
 profound reconfiguration of the visual world. During this period marked by
  civil transformation and political upheaval\, artists\, journalists\, and
  makers had opportunities to reconstruct both individual and collective id
 entities. A century later\, Cracks & Reforms presents a distinct cross-sec
 tion of this period\, revealing global currents of migration\, modernizati
 on\, and cultural redefinition through the lens of the GW Co\nCategory: Ar
 ts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/unruly-the-
 1920s-between-revolution-and-reaction
LOCATION:George Washington University\, Washington\, DC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/unruly-the-1920s-between-revolution-and
 -reaction
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
