DESCRIPTION:Representing the culmination of nearly a year of research by m
 ore than 20 GW students and alumni\, this symposium celebrates the launch 
 of an online exhibition dedicated to the print works of Marc Chagall in th
 e GW Collection. Although his achievements as an etcher are often eclipsed
  by his renowned paintings\, stained glass\, and monumental commissions\, 
 graphic art lies at the heart of his artistic practice. This online exhibi
 tion brings together 27 etchings from the GW Collection\, 14 of which are 
 from Nikolai Gogol’s Dead Souls \, and a unique silk scarf held by the G
 eorge Washington University Museum The Textile Museum. Beyond the works in
  the GW Collection\, Washington is home to numerous Cha\nCategory: Arts & 
 Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/hidden-treasures
 -of-chagall-in-washington-dc
